      "summary": "Open consultation Updating the safety at street works and road works code of practice From: Department for Transport Published: 21 September 2026 Get emails about this page Summary Seeks views on proposed updates to the safety at street works and road works code of practice. This consultation closes at 11:59pm on 14 December 2026 Consultation description We are seeking views on proposed updates to the safety at street works and road works code of practice. The draft code of practice (which should be read alongside this consultation) provides statutory guidance on the signing, lighting and guarding of street and road works on public roads and highways to help protect workers, road users and pedestrians. The proposed updates reflect changes in legislation, guidance and working practices since the safety at street works and road works code was last updated in 2013. Feedback from this consultation will be used to ensure the revised code is clear, practical and effective for those who use it. Documents Updating the safety at street works and road works code of practice HTML Safety at street works and road works: a code of practice (draft) PDF , 4.59 MB , 158 pages This file may not be suitable for users of assistive technology. Request an accessible format If you use assistive technology (such as a screen reader) and need a version of this document in a more accessible format, please email webmasterdft@dft.gov.uk . Please tell us what format you need. It will help us if you say what assistive technology you use. Ways to respond Respond online or Email to: streetmanager@dft.gov.uk Write to: The Street Works Team 4th Floor The Colmore Building 20 Colmore Circus Queensway Birmingham B4 6AT Share this page The following links open in a new tab Share on Facebook (opens in new tab",
